1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is Vouch. A deli site whose assistant may never tell you food is safe to eat.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Nothing is ticked, so nothing is checked. No dish carries a verdict it was not asked for.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,500
Thirty-four dishes, every ingredient published. All of this works with JavaScript off.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:23,000
Tick dairy-free. Thirty-four dishes checked: fifteen unsafe, three we cannot tell, sixteen with no conflict found.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,500
The Reuben is unsafe, through Swiss cheese. The Pastrami says no conflict found. Nothing here is ever called safe.

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:37,000
And the Turkey club: dairy, through brioche bun, brioche, butter. Three steps down a chain, inside a bun, invisible in the line you would read.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
Now let a model answer. The model proposes; a deterministic gate decides.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:49,500
Here is a replayed reply giving a false all-clear. Three claims withheld: one the checker contradicted, two it could not derive. The gate suppresses true statements too.

9
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:56,000
A deliberately broken network, refused. The validator's words are quoted exactly, kept apart from ours.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:03,500
Running another site's agents asks first. It names the origin and says plainly: this runs their code in your browser.

11
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:09,500
Approved. The bakery's network loads from its own origin, and nothing it says changes a verdict.

12
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:17,000
Sixteen events, written down: every router choice, every action, every receipt. The refusal and the consent among them.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The conformance CLI checks any agentic site against the spec. Fourteen of fourteen here, and it names the six checks it did not make.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,500
Model proposes. Gate decides. Evidence survives. Apache-2.0, and live now.
